    ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{2}+1$ at the point $(2,9).$\n\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+1.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+1)=4x\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,9):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{\u2032}(2)=4(2)=8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{\u2032}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-9 & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x-2) \\\\ 8y-72 & =-x+2 \\\\ x+8\\cdot y & =74.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
